messages:
sam_dev: Hey @support — customer reported rerank results where the top item is an empty placeholder with score 1.0. They say it only happens in prod when using our TS SDK v0.9.2. Repro steps attached.

ava_support: Thanks @sam_dev. Can you paste the raw request + response (headers ok to redact) and the SDK call you used? Also which model/endpoint?

sam_dev: Sure — endpoint: POST /v1/rerank. Model: rwd-re-rank-1. Payload they sent (sanitized):

```json
{
  "query": "Find the best summary",
  "candidates": ["Summary A","Summary B","Summary C"],
  "metadata": {"job_id":"s-123"}
}
```

Response (server returned top index 3 with score 1.0):

```json
{
  "scores": [0.12, 0.08, 0.09, 1.0],
  "order": [0,2,1,3]
}
```

Note the extra candidate at index 3 is not in the original payload. We only see this when customers use our TS SDK bundle (Node 18). Direct curl -> API doesn't reproduce.

leo_sdk: I can reproduce locally with ts-sdk v0.9.2 and our local stub. Looks like a padding helper we added for batching is appending null placeholders to the candidates array to align to multiples of 8. The server used to ignore nulls, but a change in the parsing layer now maps null->default_candidate with score 1.0 in the returned list.

sam_dev: Ugh. Any chance it's a user patch or bundler quirk that turns null into empty string?

leo_sdk: Here's the minimal repro I used in node: 

```js
import { rerank } from '@redwood/sdk';

await rerank({
  model: 'rwd-re-rank-1',
  query: 'Find best',
  candidates: ['A','B','C'],
});
// internals: padCandidates pads to multiple of 8: [ 'A','B','C', null, null, null, null, null ]
```

And the problematic helper (v0.9.2):

```js
function padCandidates(arr) {
  const pad = (8 - (arr.length % 8)) % 8;
  for (let i = 0; i < pad; i++) arr.push(null);
  return arr;
}
```

We then send that array unchanged; server-side change introduced a mapping where nulls are treated as implicit candidate with score=1.0 in some code paths.

ava_support: Thanks @leo_sdk — can you confirm whether Python SDK is affected? Customer says py-sdk works fine.

leo_sdk: Confirmed — py-sdk filters nulls before sending. This is a regression only in ts-sdk where padding got added but null filtering was dropped in the optimize/batching refactor.

maria_oncall: Workarounds: 1) Ask customer to pin SDK to 0.9.1 or use py-sdk for now. 2) Temporary server-side mitigation: we'll ignore trailing null/empty candidates for rerank responses if candidates_count < scores_length. I'll open a quick rule in the request parser.

leo_sdk: Plan: I'll push a hotfix to ts-sdk main to remove padCandidates or filter out nulls before network send. Will cut v0.9.3 patch in ~1.5h. Patch diff:

```diff
- body.candidates = padCandidates(body.candidates);
+ body.candidates = padCandidates(body.candidates).filter(Boolean);
```

This should be safe.

ava_support: ETA and customer communication?

leo_sdk: ETA ~90 minutes to release and publish. I'll post the release PR and changelog here when done.

maria_oncall: I'll add a server-side guard now to ignore null candidates for any rerank request handled in the next hour. Deploy-bot will post status.

deploy-bot: deploy queued: bypass-null-rerank-filter -> staging -> in progress :hourglass_flowing_sand:

sam_dev: Thank you — I'll tell the customer the bug is identified, workaround available (pin 0.9.1 or use py-sdk), and a patch + server guard are rolling out. I'll follow up when fix is live. :pray:
